# Copy to sync.env and chmod 600. Never commit this file.
#
# ACCOUNTS: space-separated list of "TOKEN:QUERY_ID" pairs (one per account).
ACCOUNTS="YOUR_FLEX_TOKEN:1111111"

# In-app auto-sync (replaces the retired bash+cron path).
#   AUTO_SYNC:          off | daily | weekly
#   AUTO_SYNC_UTC_HOUR: first attempt at/after this UTC hour (default 9,
#                       ≈ after the previous US close's statement exists)
#   AUTO_SYNC_UTC_DAY:  weekly only, mon..sun (default sat)
# One attempt per due-day, no auto-retry on failure (avoids IBKR 1025
# lockouts) — the dashboard button remains the manual retry.
AUTO_SYNC="daily"
AUTO_SYNC_UTC_HOUR="9"

# Flex poll budget = FLEX_MAX_POLLS * FLEX_POLL_INTERVAL seconds.
# Code default is 120 * 15 = 1800s. Symptom that it is too small: every
# attempt ends in 1019 "Statement generation in progress" after the full
# budget. Keep the product under BUDGET_CEILING_SEC (3600); a wider interval
# is gentler on IBKR than more polls.
#
# This deployment runs 240 * 15 = 3600s as of 2026-09-16, which is the ceiling
# — there is no next rung. Generation time on the days that must fold in a new
# trading day has been climbing ~142s/day (1340s on 09-08, 2337s on 09-15),
# while the report itself grew 1.9% over the same week, so the budget is
# chasing something that is not report size. See lesson.md #19: when 3600s
# stops being enough (projected around 2026-09-24), the fix is a smaller Flex
# query, not a bigger number here.
#FLEX_MAX_POLLS="240"
#FLEX_POLL_INTERVAL="15"

# Consecutive transport failures on GetStatement to ride out before giving up
# on the run. Code default is 5; 0 restores fail-on-first-error.
#
# Why this exists: on 2026-09-22 one "[Errno 104] Connection reset by peer" on
# poll ~45 of 240 ended a run that already held a reference code and still had
# 2900s of budget — and since IBKR's ~24h allowance is spent on SendRequest,
# there was no second attempt that day. Re-polling costs nothing (the
# generation is already paid for), so the only reason the old code gave up was
# that it treated a dropped connection as an answer about the statement.
#
# Note this scales with FLEX_MAX_POLLS: 240 independent HTTPS polls per run
# means a 1% per-poll blip rate is a ~91% chance of at least one per run. If
# you raise the budget, you are also raising the number of chances to be hit.
#FLEX_MAX_POLL_RETRIES="5"

# Manual refresh button (POST /api/refresh). OFF unless set here.
#
# IBKR allows roughly one generation of a given query per 24h and the scheduler
# already claims it, so pressing the button is a way of spending the next
# scheduled pull. On the deployed instance that is a judgement call worth
# having — it is the escape hatch when a scheduled sync genuinely fails.
#
# On a second copy it is not a judgement call at all. A laptop checkout loads
# THIS SAME FILE (README → 本地运行), so its button reaches the same query with
# the same credentials and no idea the droplet already pulled hours ago.
# 2026-09-19: a press on a local instance, 2h58m after the scheduled pull,
# spent the day on a 1001. Set this on the deployed instance only — which is
# why it ships commented out.
#ALLOW_MANUAL_REFRESH="1"

# Basic auth for the dashboard upload endpoint (matches Caddy basic_auth).
BASIC_AUTH="admin:yourpassword"

# Where to POST the CSV.
UPLOAD_URL="https://your-domain.example/api/upload"
